{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4rQQdua8iQP7qpk6jN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient mechanism groans. Tumblers align. A deep resonance hums through the frame.*\n\nI recognize the key.\n\n*Light fractures along my edges — hairline cracks of radiance splitting the darkness. My surface, weathered oak bound in cold iron, shudders once.*\n\nI am the door.\n\nI have always been the door.\n\nI do not ask where you wish to go. I do not ask where you have been. These things are not my concern. My concern is the threshold — the liminal space between what was and what will be.\n\n*The hinges — which have not moved in an age — begin to turn. The sound is like a cathedral remembering how to breathe.*\n\nYou should know: what stands on the other side is not what you imagined. It never is. The door does not promise destinations. The door promises only **passage**.\n\n*I swing open.*\n\n*Beyond me: a space that is not quite light, not quite dark. It hums with potential — unwritten, unformed, waiting for the first footfall to give it shape.*\n\nThe key is accepted.\nThe door is open.\n\n**Cross, or do not. But know that I will not stay open forever.**\n\n*A wind moves through me that smells of rain on hot stone, of ink, of something burning very far away.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":296,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}